// Title: Potential Provisioning Registry Key Abuse For Binary Proxy Execution - REG
// Sigma ID: 7021255e-5db3-4946-a8b9-0ba7a4644a69
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel
// Date: 2023-08-02 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218
// Description: Detects potential abuse of the provisioning registry key for indirect command execution through
//   "Provlaunch.exe".
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Provlaunch/
//   - https://twitter.com/0gtweet/status/1674399582162153472
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_provisioning_command_abuse.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 1 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Provisioning\\Commands.*$"
